# Todo reminders & recurrence

Recurring todo = **habit series**, not a one-shot row that mutates forever.

## Model
- `reminder` time-of-day (+ weekday / day-of-month) = series template
- `completed` = done for **current period only** (today / this ISO week / this month)
- `last_completed_at` + `todo_completion_log` = history (calendar green ticks)
- `notified_at` = last notify for current `reminder` slot

## Flow
1. `Recurrence.rolloverIfNeeded` on list/get + `@Scheduled` 60s
2. Due = `reminder <= now` AND `completed=0` AND (`notified_at` null OR `< reminder`)
3. Notify → set `notified_at` only. **Do not advance reminder.**
4. `toggleComplete` on recurring: log + `completed=true` + `reminder` → next slot
5. Next day/week/month: rollover sets `completed=false`, `reminder` = current slot

## UI
- Strikethrough only if done this period (`todo.completed` after rollover)
- Always show **last** (`lastCompletedAt`) + **next** (`reminder`)
- Calendar expand from `createdAt`, not rolled reminder; green only from completion log

## Do not
```java
// BAD — completed stuck forever / double-advance
todoMapper.markReminderNotified(id, now);
advanceRecurringIfNeeded(todo, now);
todo.setCompleted(true); // never cleared on new day
```

```java
// GOOD
Recurrence.rolloverIfNeeded(todo, now);
todoMapper.markReminderNotified(id, now); // notify only
```
